  "worked_solution": "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a\\le X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1\\le X<2) & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{4}{27}(3{x}^{2}-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{27}{\\int }_{1}^{2}3{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{27}{[{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{27}([(2)^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}(2)^{4}]-[(1)^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}(1)^{4}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{27}(8-4-\\frac{3}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{27}\\cdot \\frac{13}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{27}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
